# Generated by cargo-fuzz. None of it is source.
#
# `corpus/` is the accumulated set of inputs libFuzzer found interesting. It
# grows without bound across runs and is machine-specific, so it is rebuilt
# rather than tracked. If a corpus is worth keeping, `cargo fuzz cmin <target>`
# minimizes it first.
corpus/

# `artifacts/` holds one file per crash, timeout, or leak. These are worth
# keeping, but not here: the durable form of a fuzz finding is a named
# regression test in the crate that owns the code, asserting the real values.
# See `docs/internal/fuzzing.md`.
artifacts/

# `coverage/` is the raw profdata from `cargo fuzz coverage`.
coverage/

target/
Cargo.lock
